Join-quality metrics

Track per join:

   - stable-ID coverage
   - exact-match rate
   - alias/fuzzy-match rate
   - geospatial-only match rate
   - unresolved rate
   - one-to-many ambiguity rate
   - source disagreement rate
   - ownership/name-change survival
   - taxonomy reconciliation loss
   - manual-review precision by confidence bucket
   - identity continuity over 1d/7d/30d

For inferred edges, never collapse provenance. CONFIRMED requires
source-native identity or deterministic official-key match. INFERRED
requires explicit matching method and confidence. UNKNOWN is preserved
rather than forced.
MOT correction / moat test

DVSA=E2=80=99s MOT History API covers vehicle/test history back to 2005 for
cars/motorcycles/vans and exposes bulk + delta files. Delta files contain a
complete vehicle record, including test history, whenever a vehicle is
created, updated or deleted. Therefore POW cannot justify continuous MOT
collection merely as historical preservation.

Use MOT instead as a public outcome label:
vehicle registration -> defect/advisory -> inferred repair interval ->
later MOT result/mileage.

A proprietary moat requires the missing intervention: consenting repair
invoice/part receipt, agent-booked repair, or workshop outcome. Without
that, the repair itself remains latent.
