Exact source stack
<p><strong>Street Manager Event API</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Official guidance: <a href=3D"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/find-and-use-=
roadworks-data">https://www.gov.uk/guidance/find-and-use-roadworks-data</a>=
</li>
<li>API surface includes permit/activity <code>event_reference</code>, <cod=
e>event_type</code>, work/activity reference, coordinates, proposed and act=
ual dates, status, traffic-management type, USRN, <code>event_time</code>, =
<code>object_reference</code>, and <code>version</code>.</li>
<li>Current v7 sandbox Swagger exposes <code>GET /works/updates</code>, <co=
de>POST /permits/search</code>, plus <code>/api-notifications/subscribe</co=
de>, <code>/unsubscribe</code>, and <code>/subscriptions</code>.</li>
<li>Public roadworks data is free to view via API; account/API access is th=
e realistic permission path.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Bus Open Data Service (BODS)</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Official guidance: <a href=3D"https://www.gov.uk/guidance/find-and-use-=
bus-open-data">https://www.gov.uk/guidance/find-and-use-bus-open-data</a></=
li>
<li>Local bus timetable/location/fares data in England is freely available =
for commercial and non-commercial reuse.</li>
<li>Vehicle locations use SIRI-VM. Operators must publish location updates =
every 10=E2=80=9330 seconds; the profile contains <code>VehicleJourneyRef</=
code>, <code>VehicleRef</code>, <code>RecordedAtTime</code>, coordinates an=
d journey/call information.</li>
<li>API consumers register for an account/key. DfT warns abusive overuse ca=
n lead to access being switched off, so POW should use a bounded regional c=
ollector first.</li>
</ul>

Canonical identity graph
<p><code>StreetManager.object_reference/version -&gt; USRN + geometry -&gt;=
 affected road segment -&gt; route geometry -&gt; VehicleJourneyRef -&gt; V=
ehicleRef(day-scoped) -&gt; scheduled calls -&gt; observed SIRI-VM trajecto=
ry</code></p>
<p>Every edge stores <code>status =E2=88=88 {CONFIRMED, INFERRED, UNKNOWN}<=
/code>, <code>confidence</code>, <code>method</code>, <code>source</code>, =
<code>observed_at</code>, and raw provenance.</p>
<p>Important identity semantics:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>object_reference + version</code> =3D intervention version identi=
ty.</li>
<li>USRN is the stable street join but geometry is required because one USR=
N can cover more road than the actual works footprint.</li>
<li><code>VehicleJourneyRef</code> is the preferred operational journey key=
 and is defined to correspond to timetable identity.</li>
<li><code>VehicleRef</code> must be consistent through the day, but should =
not be assumed to be a permanent physical-bus identity across days without =
additional evidence.</li>
</ul>

